WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.320
Why would a cell make a protein all day, only to destroy it?

2
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.980
Most of your cells do exactly that with a protein called β-catenin.

3
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.380
Unless a signal tells them to stop, they destroy it soon after it is made.

4
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.400
That looks like waste.

5
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.020
It is a design.

6
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:28.353
Picture a bathtub with the tap running and the drain open.

7
00:00:29.053 --> 00:00:31.093
The water level depends on both.

8
00:00:32.153 --> 00:00:37.693
The steady level of β-catenin is its rate of synthesis divided by its rate

9
00:00:37.693 --> 00:00:38.993
constant of destruction.

10
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:45.833
Slow the destruction ten-fold, and the level rises ten-fold, with no change in how

11
00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:47.373
fast the protein is made.

12
00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.907
Take a cell that receives no signal.

13
00:00:51.727 --> 00:00:57.147
Every free copy of β-catenin meets the destruction complex, where the scaffold

14
00:00:57.147 --> 00:01:00.067
Axin holds two kinases beside it.

15
00:01:00.747 --> 00:01:07.427
CK1 puts a phosphate on serine 45, which primes GSK3 to add three more.

16
00:01:08.247 --> 00:01:14.367
A protein called β-TrCP reads the phosphates on serines 33 and 37.

17
00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:20.687
It belongs to SCF, a ligase that adds a chain of ubiquitin, and the proteasome

18
00:01:20.687 --> 00:01:21.887
destroys the protein.

19
00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:28.867
That signal is a Wnt, a protein that one cell secretes and a nearby cell reads.

20
00:01:29.727 --> 00:01:35.847
Its receptor is Frizzled, and Wnt brings it together with a partner, LRP5 or 6.

21
00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:42.027
Frizzled recruits a protein called Dishevelled, and the tail of LRP6 is

22
00:01:42.027 --> 00:01:44.627
phosphorylated and then binds Axin.

23
00:01:45.427 --> 00:01:50.127
The destruction complex is pulled to the receptor, and there it stops delivering

24
00:01:50.127 --> 00:01:51.587
β-catenin to the ligase.

25
00:01:52.307 --> 00:01:58.417
How it is stopped is still argued, but newly made β-catenin survives and builds up.

26
00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:05.157
In the nucleus, a protein called TCF sits on the DNA of Wnt target genes.

27
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:08.557
It sits there whether or not a signal has come.

28
00:02:09.397 --> 00:02:15.197
Without β-catenin, TCF holds a co-repressor called Groucho and keeps those

29
00:02:15.197 --> 00:02:21.357
genes off. The β-catenin that builds up enters the nucleus, displaces Groucho

30
00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:24.237
and brings in the proteins that start transcription.

31
00:02:24.237 --> 00:02:28.637
So TCF turns from a repressor into an activator.

32
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:34.417
Without a signal, the drain stays open and the level stays low.

33
00:02:35.457 --> 00:02:39.297
With Wnt, the drain is plugged and the level rises.

34
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:44.257
The control is on destruction, not on synthesis.

35
00:02:45.477 --> 00:02:51.417
A protein that is always made and always destroyed can be raised by one move.

36
00:02:52.337 --> 00:02:53.317
Stop the destruction.
